  ('p13', 'Counter Top', 'Marble + Steel', 'Crafted from natural stone, a marble countertop brings timeless elegance and luxury to any space with its unique, organic veining patterns. While it requires ca', 'An elegant fusion of natural history and high-end design, a marble countertop is one of the most prestigious architectural surfaces you can introduce to a home. Formed over millions of years through the intense heat and pressure of metamorphic transformation, every single slab of marble is completely unique—a geological thumbprint that cannot be perfectly replicated by any engineered alternative.

Key Visual & Physical Characteristics:
Distinctive Aesthetic: Marble is celebrated for its soft, luminous glow and signature veining patterns, which range from bold, dramatic lightning-strike lines to delicate, wispy ribbons. Its color palette spans from classic bright whites (like Carrara or Calacatta) to deep, moody charcoals, rich greens, and warm creams.

The Finish Options: Depending on the design goal, marble can be finished in two primary ways:

Polished: A high-gloss finish that maximizes light reflection and makes the colors pop.

Honed: A smooth, matte finish that offers a softer appearance and hides scratches or imperfections more effectively.

Naturally Cool Temperature: The dense stone dissipates heat rapidly, keeping its surface naturally cool to the touch. This functional trait makes it highly favored by professional bakers and pastry chefs, as dough won''t stick or melt easily during rolling.

Patina, Care, and Maintenance
While undeniably stunning, marble is a premium material that requires mindful maintenance. Because it is a calcareous natural stone composed primarily of calcium carbonate, it is porous and relatively soft compared to granite or quartz.

Understanding Etching: Marble reacts chemically when it comes into contact with acidic substances like lemon juice, vinegar, wine, or tomato sauce. This reaction causes "etching"—a dulling of the surface polish. Many homeowners view this evolving patina as a beautiful, historic characteristic that tells the story of a well-lived home, much like old European bistro tables.

To preserve its pristine condition, marble countertops must be sealed periodically (typically every 6 to 12 months) to provide a defensive barrier against deep liquid stains. Everyday cleaning requires nothing more than warm water and a pH-neutral stone cleaner; harsh chemical abrasives must be avoided.

Ultimately, investing in a marble countertop is a commitment to celebrating natural artistry. It serves as a striking, durable centerpiece that anchors a room in classic luxury, elevating the overall value and character of the space.', 15000, NULL, 'Tables', '["Handcrafted"]'::jsonb, '["Large"]'::jsonb, 50, '{"h":36,"w":12,"d":3}'::jsonb, 'from-stone-50 to-stone-200', 'https://i.pinimg.com/1200x/23/9c/32/239c328b136628d9ca9ccb1d9490c23c.jpg', '["https://i.pinimg.com/736x/ee/94/32/ee943249400a5bf2c9dc360dd1d31d62.jpg"]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, '["One-of-a-Kind Artistry: Every slab features unique, organic veining patterns and a luminous depth that engineered materials simply cannot replicate.","The Baker''s Choice: Naturally cool to the touch, the dense surface dissipates heat rapidly, making it the ideal workstation for working with delicate doughs and pastries.","A Living Finish: Over time, it develops a character-rich patina that chronicles the life of your home, echoing the classic look of historic European architecture."]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Crafted from natural stone, a marble countertop brings timeless elegance and luxury to any space with its unique, organic veining patterns. While it requires care to prevent etching and stains, its cool surface and classic aesthetic make it a highly desirable focal point for kitchens and baths.', '2026-07-04T13:34:35.117Z', '2026-07-04T13:40:20.114Z')
